--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Third-party components
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

This project has NO third-party runtime dependencies.

- The DeepSeek Harness host plugin (`plugin/`) uses only Node.js built-in modules
  (`node:fs`, `node:path`, `node:url`, `node:http`, `node:crypto`). It does not
  bundle or require any npm package at runtime.

- The WebSocket server in `plugin/lib/ws.js` is an original implementation of the
  server side of RFC 6455. No WebSocket library (`ws`, `socket.io`, `uWebSockets`)
  is included or required.

- The Edge extension (`extension/`) uses only browser platform APIs
  (`chrome.tabs`, `chrome.scripting`, `chrome.debugger`, `chrome.storage`,
  `chrome.alarms`, `chrome.notifications`, `chrome.runtime`). Manifest V3,
  Chrome 116+ API surface.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Development-only tooling
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The test suites under `tools/` run on Node.js 18+ (or on the Node runtime
embedded in DeepSeek Harness via `ELECTRON_RUN_AS_NODE=1`). They likewise
import only standard library modules. `tools/test-page-in-edge.mjs` launches
Microsoft Edge in headless mode over the Chrome DevTools Protocol; Microsoft
Edge is not redistributed here and is governed by its own license.

`tools/make-icons.py` produces the extension icons. The generated PNG files in
`extension/icons/` are original artwork created for this project.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Acknowledgements
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The capability-negotiation handshake (`caps` in the hello frame, `HOST_CAPS` on
the host side), the `expect`-before-acting guard, and the three-valued
`effect_state` receipt were designed after studying Tencent/BrowserSkill
(https://github.com/Tencent/BrowserSkill, MIT). No code was copied from that
project; the mechanisms were re-implemented for this plugin's much smaller
surface. Its Agent Window, session/borrow model, ref store, network capture,
video recording, audit log and remote-server mode are deliberately not present
here.

